In article <1993Feb18.093621.2213@Informatik.TU-Muenchen.DE> Oliver Schoett <schoett@informatik.tu-muenchen.de> writes:
>
>This is all very nice, but how do I *get* my items blessed?
>In particular, how can I turn water into holy water?

If you dip an item into holy water, it will be blessed (if it was
uncursed; the item will be uncursed if it was cursed), and one potion
of holy water will be used up. "Item" here actually means "all items
in that slot". That is, if slot "a" in your inventory is "12 potions
of water", and you dip "a" into holy water, all twelve will turn into
holy water (and one potion of holy water will be used up), giving you
a net profit of 11 holy waters.

There are other ways to bless items. For example, blessed scrolls of
enchant weapon/armor will usually bless the weapon/armor they're cast
on.
